<LegalPage title="Accessibility" updated="November 2026" description="Inge Performance Lab's commitment to an accessible website." intro="Inge Performance Lab wants every athlete and family to be able to use this website, including people who rely on assistive technology.">
  <h2>Our goal</h2>
  <p>We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA. That includes readable color contrast, keyboard navigation, descriptive text for images, captions or text alternatives where we can, and respect for reduced motion settings.</p>
  <h2>What we have done</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Built the site with semantic headings, labels and landmarks so screen readers can navigate it.</li>
    <li>Made menus, sliders and forms usable with a keyboard.</li>
    <li>Paused or removed motion for visitors who turn on reduced motion.</li>
    <li>Added alternative text to meaningful images.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <p>Some content comes from third parties, such as our Swift booking pages and embedded reviews, and may not fully meet these standards. We are working with those providers where we can.</p>
  <h2>Need help or found a problem?</h2>
  <p>If anything on this site is hard to use, tell us. We will work with you to get you the information or booking you need another way.</p>
